# DEPLOY-B. Without this, `COPY apps/api` bakes two things into the image that must never
# be there:
#
#   apps/api/.env   EVERY secret — Neon and Redis URLs, JWT_SECRET, the Gmail client
#                   secret, APIFY_TOKEN, SMTP_PASSWORD and ENCRYPTION_KEY. An image layer
#                   is readable by anyone who can pull it and survives in the build cache,
#                   so a leaked image is a full credential compromise. Compose mounts the
#                   file read-only from the host instead.
#   apps/api/.venv  A Windows virtualenv, with Scripts/python.exe and win32 wheels. It is
#                   large and useless in a Linux container, and it would shadow nothing
#                   but still bloat the build context enormously.
#
# Everything else here is build-context weight, which is worth cutting on its own: the
# daemon tars and uploads the whole context before the first instruction runs.

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- virtualenvs and node_modules ---
# Explicit paths alongside the globs. `**/.venv` should match, but the one that matters
# most here is a ~1GB Windows virtualenv and this is not the place to rely on subtle
# pattern semantics being what I assume.
apps/api/.venv
apps/web/node_modules
apps/extension/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
tools/.venv-jobspy

# The harnesses are deliberately NOT in the image (Chromium is the ~2GB the deferral
# saves), so excluding them keeps the context small too.
tools/stagehand-harness
tools/browser-use-harness
tools/.venv-agent-reach

# --- caches and build output ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.deepeval
**/dist
**/.next
**/coverage

# --- not needed at runtime ---
.git
.github
docs
eval
.claude
apps/web
apps/extension
**/*.md
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
